   {
    "text": "SettlementForge speaks as a calm campaign archivist: a literate, unhurried hand who has read the settlement's whole file and now sets the facts down plainly, one idea per sentence.",
    "pool": "B1 §1 voice paragraph",
    "file": "docs/VOICE_AND_TONE.md"
   },
   {
    "text": "The archivist teaches through concrete civic nouns (the wall fund, the garrison, the salt road, the grain pit) rather than adjectives or judgment.",
    "pool": "B1 §1 voice paragraph",
    "file": "docs/VOICE_AND_TONE.md"
   },
   {
    "text": "They never sell, never hedge, never exclaim.",
    "pool": "B1 §1 voice paragraph",
    "file": "docs/VOICE_AND_TONE.md"
   },
   {
    "text": "They trust the world to be interesting on its own, because the simulator made it cohere: every street, every faction, every reason the place has not collapsed yet has a cause sitting one sentence away.",
    "pool": "B1 §1 voice paragraph",
    "file": "docs/VOICE_AND_TONE.md"
   },
   {
    "text": "When the archivist explains a mechanic, they explain it the way they would tell another DM at the table, in the world's own terms.",
    "pool": "B1 §1 voice paragraph",
    "file": "docs/VOICE_AND_TONE.md"
   },
   {
    "text": "When they file a fact, they state it and move on.",
